--
C++20 <vector>: push_back + size.

Reclassified CORE -> KNOWNBUG by the member-typedef conformance fix
([temp.inst]/1-2, [dcl.typedef]).  Previously this passed only because the
non-conformant *truncated* std::vector had its operations havoc'd: symex
executed 0 instructions of the real container, so the property was vacuous
(cf. cpp20_erase_if, where even `v.size() == 999` "verified").  The fix makes
the front end conformant -- the class keeps its full member set (non-POD with
constructors) and symex now executes the REAL std::vector machinery (exactly the
functions g++ -O0 emits) -- but symex of the fully-elaborated container does not
complete within resources.

This is a second-tier verification-PERFORMANCE item (symex on real libstdc++
containers), not a conformance one; the previous "pass" was unsound.  Reclassify
back to CORE once symex is tractable on the real container.
See doc/architectural/cpp-class-template-instantiation-plan.md.
